invariant: INV-44
file: p384_wide_point.c
catches: p384_equiv_test
reason: the addition answers infinity for two equal points, where the
  sum is their double. With the key G and equal scalars the first
  digit of the second scalar adds the point the first one just added.
  bin/p384_equiv_test verifies that signature and wants 1.

--- old
        if (p384_wide_is_zero(rr)) {
            point_double(o, a);
        } else {
            memset(o, 0, sizeof *o);
        }
--- new
        if (p384_wide_is_zero(rr)) {
            memset(o, 0, sizeof *o);
        } else {
            memset(o, 0, sizeof *o);
        }
